# Milky Way and detailed cloud density v03

Asset: `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/PaintedCloud/v04/Altitude/Cloud3_Wisp/T_Cloud3_MilkyWay_CloudMask_v03`.

RGB is bit-identical to v02. A is repainted fine cirrus density, packed into the same upper-hemisphere region with seam fades. Delivery is 4096 x 2048 half-float EXR resampled from generated artwork. Original independent cloud RGB shading cannot fit into a single mask; shading is reconstructed from the square root of A to retain faint filaments.

Galaxy radiance is restored within the cloud3 composite so cloud3 alpha no longer attenuates the galaxy contribution. Foreground cloud1/2 occlusion remains. Night gating remains enabled. BP `Milky Way` controls now include `MilkyWayOpacity`, `MilkyWayContrast`, and `MilkyWayBrightness` (all default 1), plus existing rotation and intensity.

Validation: three material compiles passed; BP compiled without errors. Live MID readback verified all three new controls and restored prior values. Dependency audit passed. Source-over alpha compensation checked numerically; no final night viewport comparison was performed.

Built-in imagegen edit prompt: Repaint the original Wisp_Generated_Source.png as a high quality monochrome SINGLE CHANNEL DENSITY texture. Preserve flowing long feathery cirrus curl silhouettes and detailed delicate brush filaments, broad panoramic distribution. Pure opaque black background, white bright filaments, gray thin density. No transparency/checkerboard. Encode all internal cloud texture with crisp slender wispy filaments, soft boundaries and dark gaps, not uniform grey fog or blurred lumps. No cumulus scallops, sawteeth, stars or nebula. Wide 2:1 canvas, cloud band across middle, black top/bottom margins and faded left/right seam margins.
